.nh
.TH "PB-PREVIEW" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview - Expose a local target through a temporary preview


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview <port|url|path> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Expose a local target through a temporary preview URL. The target is a bare port (3000
means http://127.0.0.1:3000), an http, https, h2c or tcp URL with an explicit port and nothing
else (no path, query or user), or an absolute Unix socket path (also written unix:///path).

.PP
A preview is public by default. --private limits it to your account and --team requires an
explicit team grant (they cannot be combined). --ttl limits its lifetime to at most 24h.
--host-header sends a different Host to the origin, for servers that allow-list one (http, https
and h2c targets; give a bare name without a port). --domain attaches a verified custom domain
and waits up to 15 minutes for its DNS and certificate.

.PP
The preview runs while the command runs; Ctrl+C stops it. --background hands it to this
computer's background service and returns once it is ready, with a default lifetime of 30
minutes.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--background\fP[=false]
	hand the preview to this computer's background service and return once ready (default lifetime 30m)

.PP
\fB--domain\fP=[]
	attach a verified custom domain (repeatable)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for preview

.PP
\fB--host-header\fP=""
	send this Host to the origin instead of the public host (http, https, h2c targets; for dev servers with a host allow-list)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the canonical preview resource as JSON

.PP
\fB--private\fP[=false]
	limit the preview to this account

.PP
\fB--team\fP[=false]
	require an explicit team grant for browser access

.PP
\fB--ttl\fP=0s
	bounded preview lifetime (maximum 24h)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb preview 3000
  pb preview https://127.0.0.1:8443 --private --ttl 2h
  pb preview unix:///run/app.sock --host-header myapp.test
  pb preview 3000 --background --json
.EE


